# Local environment template.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# then fill in the values below. `.env` and every other `.env.*` variant are
# gitignored; this file is the only one that is tracked, and it must never
# carry a real value.
#
# Everything here is read at BUILD time. The site is static — there is no
# server runtime to read environment variables in — so these values are baked
# into the generated HTML. Nothing here can be a secret, and the schema in
# astro.config.ts marks them `access: 'public'` to say so out loud.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CLOSEBOT_SOURCE — the chat widget's Sales Pixel id
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# WHERE TO GET IT, in CloseBot:
#
#   Source Settings  →  Setup  →  Sales Pixel
#
# Copy the id from there. It is the value interpolated into the widget's script
# URL as `?source=...` — hence the variable name, which matches the query
# parameter rather than CloseBot's UI label for it.
#
# NOT A SECRET. It ends up in a <script src> that every visitor receives, so
# `view-source:` on any deployed page shows it. Keeping it out of the
# repository is about FORK HYGIENE, not secrecy: without this, anyone who
# clones the repo and deploys it loads *this* account's agent, and a stranger's
# visitors — plus the usage they generate — land in someone else's CloseBot.
#
# LEAVE IT EMPTY AND NO WIDGET RENDERS. That is the correct default for a fork
# or a contributor, and the test suite adapts to it instead of failing: the
# script-count assertion derives its expected number from whether the widget is
# present. Everything else — the site, the budgets, the SEO suite — works
# without it.
#
# WHERE IT IS SET FOR REAL (all three, or that surface loses the widget):
#
#   Cloudflare  →  Workers & Pages → brycedecora → Settings → Builds
#                  → Variables and secrets, as type "Variable"
#                  Set it under BOTH tabs: "Production" and "Previews Base".
#                  They are separate lists; filling in only one leaves PR
#                  preview deploys with no widget.
#
#   GitHub      →  Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions → Variables
#                  (a *variable*, not a secret — it is public by construction)
#                  Note: GitHub does not pass variables to workflows triggered
#                  by a PR from a fork, so an outside contributor's CI builds
#                  without the widget. That is expected and handled.
#
# A missing value fails QUIETLY — no widget, no build error. After a deploy,
# confirm with:
#
#   curl -s https://brycedecora.com/ | grep -o 'cb.js?source=[^"]*'
#
CLOSEBOT_SOURCE=
